    "section": "Reading",
    "passage": "I have never been good at sports, so you can imagine how nervous I was when my neighbour invited me to join Riverside Sports Club, a small community club in our town. My golden rule of free time has always been to avoid any activity where I might embarrass myself in front of strangers. Still, the club offered a beginners' badminton course on Saturday mornings, and the first month was free, so I decided to give it a try.<br><br>On my first day, the coach did not ask us to play a match. Instead of competing, we spent the whole session learning how to hold the racket, move our feet, and serve. Besides badminton, the club also runs table tennis, swimming and yoga classes, and members can use the small gym at no extra cost. Whenever I made a mistake, the coach corrected me patiently, and the other beginners cheered me on. I was both embarrassed and delighted.<br><br>We finished at noon, and then everyone stayed for tea in the club café, chatting like old friends. Six months later, I still can't win a match, but I have never felt healthier or happier.",
