    "n": 17,
    "type": "mcq",
    "section": "Cloze",
    "passage": "Urban gardening has changed the way city people think about food and green space. Growing vegetables at home makes city dwellers <b>(17)&nbsp;___</b> more connected to nature, even when they live far from the countryside. Although planting in small spaces is not new, modern tools and online guides have made urban gardening more popular, cheaper to start, and <b>(18)&nbsp;___</b> to manage. As a result, gardens have appeared on balconies, rooftops and school playgrounds. <b>(19)&nbsp;___</b> a rooftop garden is planted, it continues to cool the building below and clean the air around it. Regular time spent among plants can also improve a person's <b>(20)&nbsp;___</b>, reduce stress, and encourage healthier eating. More and more young people are becoming interested <b>(21)&nbsp;___</b> growing their own food instead of buying everything from supermarkets. <b>(22)&nbsp;___</b>, urban gardening even brings neighbours together, turning strangers who share a courtyard into friends who share vegetables. Therefore, every city should give its residents more space to plant.",
